================================================================================
F-1 (BLOCKING) — halt's id containment survives removal; class of 2 in this opus
================================================================================
The brief says: "--decision ... that safeItemPath(join(root, "decisions"), id) rejects
(D-008 containment — the same helper, not a fresh join)". The implementation does this
correctly (lifecycle.ts:468 opus, :491 decision). The tests cannot tell whether it does.

Instance (a): --decision. Block 19's only traversal case is "../../etc/passwd".
safeItemPath appends ".md", so a raw join resolves it to /etc/passwd.md. That file
never exists, and the existsSync refusal masks the missing containment.
  Mutant: lifecycle.ts:491  safeItemPath(join(root,"decisions"), decisionId)
                         -> join(root, "decisions", `${decisionId}.md`)
  BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR=19 lifecycle.test.ts -> 0 FAIL, exit 0 (mutant survives)
  Exploit on the mutant, sample-studio copy:
    halt W-002 --reason r --resume-when rw --decision ../leges/qa
    -> "W-002: state=halted by=../leges/qa", exit 0, halted_by: ../leges/qa written
  Real code: exit 2, file unchanged, 0 events.

Instance (b): the opus id. The brief's refusal list covers "unknown opus id, or one
safeItemPath rejects", but block 19 has no opus-id traversal case.
  Mutant: lifecycle.ts:468  safeItemPath(join(root,"opera"), opusId)
                         -> join(root, "opera", `${opusId}.md`)
  BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR=19 -> 0 FAIL (mutant survives)
  Exploit on the mutant: halt ../petitiones/A-1 --reason r --resume-when rw --decision D-1
    -> "../petitiones/A-1: state=halted by=D-1", exit 0: a petitio rewritten as halted.
  Real code: "unknown opus: ../petitiones/A-1", exit 2.

The house precedent aims traversal cases at a file that EXISTS
(lifecycle.test.ts:414 and :428 use ../../../../../etc/hostname), so that only
containment can refuse them. Instance (a) is the brief's own literal case, so the
defect started in the spec. The builder copied it faithfully, but it still does not
test the property the brief demands.

Fix, in block 19's existing table (freshStudio copies sample-studio, which has
leges/qa.md and petitiones/A-1.md):
  - { label: "--decision of ../leges/qa", opusId: "W-002", args: [...,"--decision","../leges/qa"] }
  - { label: "opus id ../petitiones/A-1", opusId: "../petitiones/A-1", args: [...good] }
Assert that exit is 2, that no event is appended, AND that the TARGET file is
unchanged: petitiones/A-1.md and opera/W-002.md. The table's current "opus file
unchanged" read uses join(dir,"opera",`${opusId}.md`), which already resolves to the
petitio for case 2, so it works if the label/path wiring is kept. Show that both
cases fail against the raw-join mutant before landing; round 2 will re-run both
mutants.

