F-3 (advisory, reasoning accepted) — what red 02 proves
================================================================================
The builder's reasoning is correct. An always-refusing stub trivially satisfies an
all-refusal table, so without a positive control `red` would refuse to record.
The brief's step 3 prescribes such a control. But the only FAILs in 02 are the
positive control ("valid case exits 0", "wrote state=halted"). Every refusal
assertion PASSes in that log. So 02 proves the block bites, not that its refusals do.
Under a stub, only an accepting mutation can make a refusal red.
Independent mutations on the real body, this round:
  m1 drop done/halted refusal  -> block 19 FAIL (caught)
  m2 drop decision existsSync  -> block 19 FAIL (caught)
  m3 halt deletes probationes  -> block 20 FAIL (caught)
  m4 halt omits halted_at      -> blocks 18, 21 FAIL (caught; halted.at fires)
  m5 ready keeps halted_by     -> block 22 FAIL (caught)
  m6/m7 raw-join containment   -> SURVIVE (F-1)
No re-record of 02 is required. The red is valid and distinct.

Note (pre-existing, not W-042): a red's "# command:" header omits
BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR, so the header alone reruns the whole file, and the
behaviour N -> block N+17 mapping lives only in the test comments. That is a
property of `red`/the W-020 harness.

